rule SEC104 "unsafe-deserialization" {
  lang python
  severity error

  find c: call where c.text ~ /\b(pickle\.loads?|marshal\.loads?|yaml\.load)\(/ and not c.text ~ /SafeLoader/
  report c "untrusted data may reach an unsafe deserializer"

  example fire python """
    data = pickle.loads(request.data)  #~ error
  """
  example clean python """
    data = json.loads(request.data)
  """
  example notapplicable markdown """
    Prose deserializes nothing.
  """
  explain """
    pickle, marshal and the default YAML loader build arbitrary objects, so a crafted request body runs code in the server (WEBSEC, registered in the SEC namespace). Other languages need an adapter and are reported Unresolved by the family, never clean.
    ## Remedy
    Parse request data with `json.loads` or `yaml.safe_load` and validate the shape with a schema.
  """
}
